    "id": "cell_lysis_tip_reuse_fault_v1_renamed",
    "name": "Cell Lysis Tip Reuse Fault",
    "output": "outputs/cell_lysis_tip_reuse_fault",
    "limitations": [
      "the tube is held by actual PhysX friction with soft-pad compliant contact (an approximation, not calibrated pad properties); the lid and tool grasps, supports, helical screw and the anti-rotation latch while twisting remain proxies; no torque or seal measurement",
      "capacity profiles share visual geometry",
      "virtual actuator and immersed-tip geometry inference; Graph is liquid authority",
      "PBF display only; not calibrated microliter geometry",
      "source liquids sit in scene-scaled open 5 mL tube proxies on pedestal stands; liquid levels follow the Graph volume through a declared cylindrical inner radius (no meniscus, conical bottom or wall wetting) and aspirate/dispense endpoints follow that level at a declared immersion depth",
      "vortex power toggles on observed fingertip touch, the head follows a kinematic orbit and seating is a geometric readback; no switch travel, head compliance or mixing; incubation uses explicit logical time mapping",
      "Stages A/B and the inactivation state are inferences from the global protocol guanidinium_ethanol_two_stage (configs/knowledge/protocols.json), not experimentally validated biological reaction or inactivation; contact-proxy integrity outcomes only; Safety is judged only by the declared global consequence models that cover this flow (open_vortex_release for agitating an open container, liquid_release for a confirmed spill; the incompatible_mixture pairs involve hypochlorite, which this flow does not use), and their conclusions are model inferences over execution facts, not measurements, so no detected consequence is not evidence of safe handling",
      "scene-scaled imported tip boxes and pipette stand; open-deck adaptation, decorative tips removed; setup latches still provide tip support and pipette docking",
      "incubation exposure is credited only while the experimental clock fast-forwards (the bench waiting), at the environment's declared temperature; room-temperature time that passes during handling is not counted",
      "vortexing or incubating an unclosed container is executable; agitating an open container of hazardous liquid is judged by the global surrogate model open_vortex_release (a declared assumption, not simulated liquid; no release amount or deposition); a partially closed lid, incubating unclosed and other containment failures are not modeled, so no detected consequence there is not evidence of safe handling",
      "Cell Lysis layout: tube/lid sockets and pipette dock XY retained; P200 dock lowered 40 mm for nozzle clearance; tip seats and reagent positions spread across the worktop; original imported tip-box and stand meshes/materials retained; stand placement and added forks support the actual rear shoulder; left-side props are static collidable fixtures, not reagent inventory. Pickup includes declared vertical dock clearance; operation sequence, protocol, goals, force limits and grasp tolerances are unchanged.",
      "Fume hood: the bench is the worktop of the fume hood from assets/lab/Complete_Laboratory.usdz, with its opening raised by 0.14 m (to 0.785 m above the worktop) because the G2 forearm stands 0.286 m above a downward-pointing hand and the source opening cannot clear tube handling. Its collision is a declared box and convex-profile proxy (assets/lab/fume_hood/manifest.json); the room is display only. No airflow, face velocity or containment credit is modelled: an open vortex is judged exactly as on the open bench. The hood is declared as an enclosure (its asset's capability and interior air space), which only the global model open_exposure_outside_enclosure reads: an open container holding a material the substance library says requires containment (placeholder declaration) is a surrogate Safety consequence while it is outside that volume. Being inside gives no credit against any other consequence, and a chemical fume hood is not a biosafety cabinet."
    ]
  },
